  Also removed [38;5;153mnotes[39m from [38;5;153mschema.sql[39m, since the README says it's kept in sync with the migrations by hand.

  Two things to be aware of before this goes out:

  - The drop is irreversible — the [38;5;153mnotes[39m data for those 48,000 production rows is gone once it runs, with no backup
    taken by the migration itself.
  - [38;5;153mALTER TABLE ... DROP COLUMN[39m requires SQLite 3.35+ (March 2021). If the deploy job runs an older SQLite, this needs
    the table-rebuild approach instead.

  I didn't run anything — there's no test or migration runner in the repo.

